module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.AssociatedModule.EssImageGlobalization
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.AssociatedModule.OpenCoverQuasicoherence
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.QuasicoherentOnSiteOfPresentation

/-!
# A global presentation on a site with a final object is a presentation

A global presentation in the sense of Stacks 03DE (6) — `SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation` —
indexes its two coproducts by types in `Type (max u v r)`, where `u` and `v` are the universes of
the objects and the morphisms of the site and `r` that of the sections.  Mathlib's
`SheafOfModules.free` is indexed by `Type r`, so on a *big* site, where `u = r + 1`, the two
notions are not interchangeable by shrinking the index types: on a big site they cannot be
shrunk at all, since `UnivLE.{r + 1, r}` is false by `not_univLE_succ`.

What makes them interchangeable all the same is that on a site with a final object the global
sections of a sheaf of modules form a `Type r`-small type — a section is determined by its value
at the final object — which is the hypothesis of
`SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation.nonempty_presentation_of_small_sections`.  This file
supplies it, and so gets a `SheafOfModules.Presentation` out of a global presentation with no size
hypothesis on the site.

The *generators* half of that is also recorded on its own, under the hypothesis of smallness of
the sections of the one module.  Writing `L` for the universe lift
`SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentation`, the presentation gives an epimorphism `b : P ⟶ L M` out of
a coproduct of copies of `L (unit R)`, so each of its components is a global section of `L M`,
hence — the lift being full — the lift of a global section of `M`.  Those sections all occur in a
`Type r`-indexed enumeration of *all* global sections of `M`, so `b` factors through the lift of
the canonical map `free I₀ ⟶ M` out of the free module on that enumeration; and the lift being
faithful, and therefore reflecting epimorphisms, that canonical map is itself an epimorphism.

## Main results

* `SheafOfModules.small_sections_of_isTerminal`: on a site with a final object the global
  sections of a sheaf of modules are `Type r`-small.
* `SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation.nonempty_generatingSections`: a sheaf of modules with a
  global presentation and `Type r`-small global sections is generated by a `Type r`-indexed
  family of global sections.
* `SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation.nonempty_presentation_of_isTerminal`: on a site with a
  final object a global presentation gives a `SheafOfModules.Presentation`, with no size
  hypothesis.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.nonempty_generatingSections_of_hasGlobalPresentation` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.nonempty_localGeneratorsData`: **on the big fppf site of a
  scheme `S` a quasi-coherent `𝒪`-module is locally generated by a `Type u`-indexed family of
  global sections**, unconditionally — even though it need not be generated by its global
  sections over `S` itself, by
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.not_exists_globalFreePresentation`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.nonempty_quasicoherentData` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isQuasicoherent_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite`: **on the big fppf
  site of `S` the quasi-coherence of Stacks 03DL(6) implies Mathlib's**, again with no size
  hypothesis.

## Implementation notes

`SheafOfModules.small_sections_of_isTerminal` is what makes the shrinking possible, and it
applies on the big fppf site of `S` and on every localization of it: the site itself has the
final object `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isTerminalOpensObjTop`, and a slice has the final
object `CategoryTheory.Over.mkIdTerminal`.  It is the reason the shrinking goes through here
where shrinking the index types does not.

The *relations* half of a presentation — generating sections of `kernel σ.π` — does not need
exactness of the universe lift.  Only the kernel of the
lifted map is ever formed, inside
`SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation.nonempty_presentation_of_small_sections`, and the global
sections of `kernel σ.π` are small for the same reason the sections of the module are, a final
object being a property of the site and not of the module.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01B4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01B4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DX)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe r v u

namespace SheafOfModules

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{r}}

/-- **On a site with a final object the global sections of a sheaf of modules are small.**  A
global section is a compatible family of local sections, and compatibility along the unique
morphism to the final object determines every member of the family from the member at the final
object; so the global sections inject into the sections over the final object, which form a type
in `Type r`. -/
public theorem small_sections_of_isTerminal {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    (M : SheafOfModules.{r} R) : Small.{r} M.sections := by
  refine small_of_injective (f := fun s : M.sections ↦ s.val (op T)) ?_
  intro s t hst
  refine Subtype.ext (funext fun X ↦ ?_)
  rw [← s.property (f := (hT.from X.unop).op), ← t.property (f := (hT.from X.unop).op)]
  exact congrArg _ hst

section Generators

variable [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{r}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{r}]

/-- **The generators of a global presentation may be taken in `Type r`.**  A sheaf of modules
with a global presentation and with `Type r`-small global sections is generated by a
`Type r`-indexed family of global sections, namely by an enumeration of *all* of its global
sections.

This is the generators half of
`SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation.nonempty_presentation_of_small_sections` with the
hypothesis `UnivLE.{max u v r, r}` replaced by smallness of the sections alone, which is
available on a big site while that hypothesis is not. -/
public theorem HasGlobalPresentation.nonempty_generatingSections {M : SheafOfModules.{r} R}
    [Small.{r} M.sections] (h : M.HasGlobalPresentation) : Nonempty M.GeneratingSections := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨I, K, P, Q, ι, κ, ⟨hP⟩, ⟨hQ⟩, a, b, hab, ⟨hb⟩⟩ := h
  set t₀ : Shrink.{r} M.sections → M.sections := fun j ↦ (equivShrink M.sections).symm j with ht₀
  set π₀ : free (R := R) (Shrink.{r} M.sections) ⟶ M := M.freeHomEquiv.symm t₀ with hπ₀
  set g : I → (unit R ⟶ M) := fun i ↦ uliftForPresentationMapDown (ι i ≫ b) with hg
  set idx : I → Shrink.{r} M.sections := fun i ↦ equivShrink M.sections (M.unitHomEquiv (g i))
    with hidx
  have hfac : ∀ i, ιFree (R := R) (idx i) ≫ π₀ = g i := by
    intro i
    rw [hπ₀, ← unitHomEquiv_symm_freeHomEquiv_apply, Equiv.apply_symm_apply, hidx, ht₀]
    simp
  set d : P ⟶ uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, max u v r} (free (R := R) (Shrink.{r} M.sections))
    := Cofan.IsColimit.desc hP
      (fun i ↦ uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r} (ιFree (idx i))) with hd
  have hdfac : ∀ i, ι i ≫ d =
      uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r} (ιFree (R := R) (idx i)) := by
    intro i
    rw [hd]
    exact Cofan.IsColimit.fac hP _ i
  have hdb : d ≫ uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r} π₀ = b := by
    refine Cofan.IsColimit.hom_ext hP _ _ fun i ↦ ?_
    rw [Limits.cofan_mk_inj, ← Category.assoc, hdfac i, ← uliftForPresentationMap_comp, hfac i, hg]
    exact uliftForPresentationMap_down _
  have hbepi : Epi b := Cofork.IsColimit.epi hb
  have hepi : Epi (uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r} π₀) := by
    rw [← hdb] at hbepi
    exact epi_of_epi d _
  exact ⟨{ I := Shrink.{r} M.sections
           s := t₀
           epi := ⟨fun {Z} p q hpq ↦ uliftForPresentationMap_injective
             ((cancel_epi (uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r} π₀)).mp (by
               rw [← uliftForPresentationMap_comp, ← uliftForPresentationMap_comp]
               exact congrArg _ hpq))⟩ }⟩

end Generators

section Presentations

variable [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{r}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{r}]

/-- **On a site with a final object a global presentation gives a
`SheafOfModules.Presentation`, with no size hypothesis.**  This is
`SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation.nonempty_presentation_of_small_sections`, whose hypothesis
is smallness of the global sections of every sheaf of modules, supplied here by
`SheafOfModules.small_sections_of_isTerminal`.

It is the full statement of which
`SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation.nonempty_generatingSections` is the generators half, and it
applies where `UnivLE.{max u v r, r}` does not: on a big site, by `not_univLE_succ`. -/
public theorem HasGlobalPresentation.nonempty_presentation_of_isTerminal {T : C}
    (hT : IsTerminal T) {M : SheafOfModules.{r} R} (h : M.HasGlobalPresentation) :
    Nonempty M.Presentation :=
  have : ∀ N : SheafOfModules.{r} R, Small.{r} N.sections :=
    fun N ↦ small_sections_of_isTerminal hT N
  h.nonempty_presentation_of_small_sections

end Presentations

end SheafOfModules

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

namespace BigFppfOver

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- The global sections of a sheaf of modules on the big fppf site of `S` are `Type u`-small: the
site has the final object `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isTerminalOpensObjTop`. -/
public theorem small_sections (G : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheaf B S hS)) :
    Small.{u} G.sections :=
  SheafOfModules.small_sections_of_isTerminal (isTerminalOpensObjTop B S hS) G

/-- The global sections of a sheaf of modules on a localization of the big fppf site of `S` are
`Type u`-small: a slice category has the final object `CategoryTheory.Over.mkIdTerminal`. -/
public theorem small_sections_over (X : BigFppfOver B S hS)
    (G : SheafOfModules.{u} ((structureSheaf B S hS).over X)) : Small.{u} G.sections :=
  SheafOfModules.small_sections_of_isTerminal Over.mkIdTerminal G

/-- **A module with a global presentation on the big fppf site of `S` is generated by a
`Type u`-indexed family of global sections.** -/
public theorem nonempty_generatingSections_of_hasGlobalPresentation
    {G : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheaf B S hS)} (h : G.HasGlobalPresentation) :
    Nonempty G.GeneratingSections :=
  have := small_sections B S hS G
  h.nonempty_generatingSections

/-- **A module with a global presentation on a localization of the big fppf site of `S` is
generated by a `Type u`-indexed family of global sections.** -/
public theorem nonempty_generatingSections_over_of_hasGlobalPresentation
    (X : BigFppfOver B S hS) {G : SheafOfModules.{u} ((structureSheaf B S hS).over X)}
    (h : G.HasGlobalPresentation) : Nonempty G.GeneratingSections :=
  have := small_sections_over B S hS X G
  h.nonempty_generatingSections

/-- **Stacks 01B4 at the big fppf site of `S`, unconditionally.**  A quasi-coherent `𝒪`-module on
`(Sch/S)_fppf` is locally generated by a `Type u`-indexed family of global sections: Stacks 03DN
produces a covering family of the final object with global presentations on its members, and on
each member those presentations are shrunk to `Type u`-indexed generating sections.

The restriction to a covering is not removable: by
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.not_exists_globalFreePresentation` a quasi-coherent module on this
site need not be generated by its global sections over `S` itself. -/
public theorem nonempty_localGeneratorsData (G : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheaf B S hS))
    (hG : G.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) : Nonempty G.LocalGeneratorsData.{u + 1} := by
  obtain ⟨I, X, hX, hP⟩ :=
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite_iff_exists_cover_hasGlobalPresentation G).1 hG
  exact ⟨{ I := I
           X := X
           coversTop := hX
           generators := fun i ↦
             (nonempty_generatingSections_over_of_hasGlobalPresentation B S hS (X i)
               (hP i)).some }⟩

/-- **A module with a global presentation on the big fppf site of `S` has a
`SheafOfModules.Presentation`.** -/
public theorem nonempty_presentation_of_hasGlobalPresentation
    {G : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheaf B S hS)} (h : G.HasGlobalPresentation) :
    Nonempty G.Presentation :=
  h.nonempty_presentation_of_isTerminal (isTerminalOpensObjTop B S hS)

/-- **A module with a global presentation on a localization of the big fppf site of `S` has a
`SheafOfModules.Presentation`.** -/
public theorem nonempty_presentation_over_of_hasGlobalPresentation (X : BigFppfOver B S hS)
    {G : SheafOfModules.{u} ((structureSheaf B S hS).over X)} (h : G.HasGlobalPresentation) :
    Nonempty G.Presentation :=
  h.nonempty_presentation_of_isTerminal Over.mkIdTerminal

/-- **Stacks 03DX at the big fppf site of `S`, unconditionally.**  A quasi-coherent `𝒪`-module on
`(Sch/S)_fppf` carries Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.QuasicoherentData`: Stacks 03DN produces a
covering family of the final object with global presentations on its members, and on each member
the global presentation becomes a `SheafOfModules.Presentation`. -/
public theorem nonempty_quasicoherentData (G : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheaf B S hS))
    (hG : G.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) : Nonempty G.QuasicoherentData.{u + 1} := by
  obtain ⟨I, X, hX, hP⟩ :=
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite_iff_exists_cover_hasGlobalPresentation G).1 hG
  exact ⟨{ I := I
           X := X
           coversTop := hX
           presentation := fun i ↦
             (nonempty_presentation_over_of_hasGlobalPresentation B S hS (X i) (hP i)).some }⟩

/-- **On the big fppf site of `S` the quasi-coherence of Stacks 03DL(6) implies Mathlib's**, with
no size hypothesis — unlike `SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite.isQuasicoherent`, whose
hypothesis `UnivLE.{u + 1, u}` is false here by `not_univLE_succ`. -/
public theorem isQuasicoherent_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite
    (G : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheaf B S hS)) (hG : G.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) :
    G.IsQuasicoherent :=
  (nonempty_quasicoherentData B S hS G hG).some.isQuasicoherent

end BigFppfOver

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
